# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Forensics / malware analysis tooling — pp-security subnet
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Label group. No play targets it; it exists so these hosts are recorded
# rather than invisible. A host absent from inventory is a host nobody
# reasons about -- see pp-dcs-ctrl, which sat with no telemetry for months
# because [ot_servers] was never made a child of [splunk-forwarder].
#
# TELEMETRY POSTURE, decided 2026-09-01: instrument what ANALYSES, not what
# DETONATES.
#   pp-sift    evidence host (disk/memory images, timelines). Executes
#              nothing hostile and holds the investigation's work product,
#              so it is a high-value target and SHOULD carry an agent --
#              the same argument recorded for [hunt] above. Not yet
#              enrolled: see the note below.
#   pp-remnux  detonation host -> [unmanaged], not enrolled
#   pp-flare   detonation host -> [unmanaged], not enrolled
#
# TO ENROL pp-sift, three things are needed and none are assumed here:
#   1. host_vars/pp-sift.yml with ansible_host and working credentials --
#      the RDP_SIFT image may not carry the simspace account group_vars/
#      linux.yml expects.
#   2. a decision NOT to add it to [linux]: that group pulls in the `common`
#      role, which performs a systemd-networkd -> NetworkManager cutover, a
#      netplan overwrite and a reboot. Appropriate for a range-built Ubuntu
#      host, not for a vendor forensics appliance.
#   3. adding `forensics` to the enrol pattern in playbooks/75-endpoint.yml
#      (`windows:linux:!unmanaged:!so_all`), which then picks up pp-sift and
#      still excludes the two detonation hosts via [unmanaged].
[forensics]
pp-sift
pp-remnux
pp-flare

